This week's announcement from IBM says that the new version will 
combine the best of AIX, SCO and Sequent's PTX.

It will support the new Intel Merced (hence the borrowing of code from 
SCO) and every RS/6000 from bottom to top. I suspect they are picking 
up the fault-tolerant code from Sequent.

This is not the death of AIX, but rather the continued evolution. And 
an attempt to be the only real competitor to linux.

