> Hello everyone,
>
> Recently, I've got a new disk and I would like to copy everything
> (bootblock, system files) from old to the new one.
> Is there any simple procedure? (I am not an expert in Dunix yet ;) ).

Take your new disk (eg rz1) and zero the disk label:
disklabel -z rz1
Use dd to copy the entire disk (eg. old disk is rz0):
dd if=/dev/rrz0c of=/dev/rrz1c bs=64k
That should do it.

Mark.


