In article <7070do$8po$1@nslave1.tin.it>,
  "Memoman" <smart@stopit.uk> wrote:
> Hi people
> I've an AlphaServer 4100 with OSF1 4.0B my question is....
> How can I get the device files for a tape installed on my system?
> I need it to make a tar !!!
> Is there a command or tool to achieve this ???
>
> Thanks in advance to all...
>
>
The tape device files will be /dev/nrmt* and /dev/rmt*. If you do not have
these files, check out your /var/adm/messages file for the the tz decive, and
do a makedev.
e.g.
If your tape is tz5 do:
cd /dev
./MAKEDEV tz5
If this is the first tape device file it will create the files /dev/rmt0* and
/dev/nrmt0*. If there are already tape device files you will get /dev/rmt1*
/dev/nrmt1* or higher nembers depending on how many have been made.
Do a file /dev/nrmt*h to check that you can see the device eg:
# file /dev/nrmt0h
/dev/nrmt0h:    character special (9/19459) SCSI #1 TZ89     tape #1 (SCSI ID
#3) (SCSI LUN #0) 85700_bpi

If you don't get the tape drive type (TZ89, in example) you may have got the
wrong tz number.

Mark.


