joshua geller (dclxvi@best.com) wrote:
: I would be satisfied knowing how to boot off a copy of the CD on an
: NFS server on the LAN. I have a SCO box that has a copy of the dist CD
: and I wondered what the procedure might be; I notice when I do 
: <show device> at the >>> prompt it lists the ethernet interface as a
: device to boot off. So how is this done?

Set up you SCO box as a bootp server, make sure it exports the proper 
root file system from CD to your alpha, set ewa0_protocols (or whichever
ethernet adapter you'd got) in the SRM console to bootp, and 'boot ewa0'.
If you set up your SCO box correctly[*] and both machines are on the same
subnet this should be enough.

Cheers,

/Serge.P

[*] Be prepared to experiment, and have a garbage bin[**] nearby.
[**] For the pulled hair, that is.



