> 
> Set up you SCO box as a bootp server, make sure it exports the proper
> root file system from CD to your alpha, set ewa0_protocols (or whichever
> ethernet adapter you'd got) in the SRM console to bootp, and 'boot ewa0'.
> If you set up your SCO box correctly[*] and both machines are on the same
> subnet this should be enough.
> 

You will need one more thing, a network bootable kernel.  I assume you
have
something running Digital UNIX already?  You can make a bootable kernel
by running doconfig  with the "-n" option.  More info in the man page
for
doconfig.  Put this kernel in /tftpboot on the sco box and put the file
name in the "bf=" field of the bootptab entry.

Once it boots with the kernel and mounts the cdrom via nfs for it's root
filesystem it should run the install.

good luck,

- Doug



