Yingwei Peng wrote:
> Recently, I tried to port my programs to OSF1 V3.2 62 alpha.
> The programs run well on Sun Solaris 2.x. I can compile them on OSF1.
> However, when I run them, I got "System terminating: bad address".

There is a very useful 'Sun Solaris to DIGITAL UNIX Porting Guide'
document which can be downloaded from:
	http://www.digital.com/hpc/ref/refdoc.html#porting

Your problem will probably be related to sizes of the various types:
check for hardcoded sizes in malloc's instead of n*sizeof(type), and for
passing an int*/float* to a function expecting long*/double*. Take note
of compiler warnings also!

Good luck,

Niel.

-- 
Niel Markwick
Consultant Software Engineer
Kontich, Belgium.



