In article <3625E795.6E0E289@vips.lpl.arizona.edu>, Vance Haemmerle <vance@vips.lpl.arizona.edu> writes:
|> I've just upgraded from DU 4.0B to 4.0D and now I'm getting crashes
|> related to PPP.  I haven't changed any PPP configuration between
|> the upgrade.  There were no problems at 4.0B.  The crash-data.xx
|> file in /var/adm/crash says the system panics with "kernel memory
|> fault".  The trace includes ip_forward.

I checked with the Digital UNIX engineers, and with Vance's help,
we apparently have confirmed that a patch for this particular
problem is in the next Digital UNIX V4.0D patch kit, which
has a code name something like "duv40das00003".

Unfortunately, it's available yet, so it's not yet online at
	http://ftp1.service.digital.com/patches/public/Digital_UNIX/v4.0d/
(the current patch kit there is duv40das00002-19980717.tar)
so if anyone else is having this particular problem, you should
probably check with the Customer Services people.

Note that the older ("duv40das00002") patch kit DOES contain
a patch for a problem involving ip_forward, but it's a different
problem.  That one seems to be limited to SMP systems.  Vance
has a uniprocessor, and the newer patch seems to have solved
his problem.

-Jeff



