Digital Unix 4.0B and better supports installation cloning and unattended
install. Very detailed and well explained in the Digital Unix Installation
Guide, Appendix C "Installation Enhancements".

Basically, the idea is that every time you install Digital unix on a machine,
the OS records its motions to a text file called install.cdf placed
automatically in /var/adm/smlogs. Later on you can edit that file to modify
instllation parameters for a future installation on a different machine,
provided you copy the install.cdf to a floppy, or to a RIS server, or to a
special directory of your distribution media (CD-ROM, tape, whatever). You also
have the option to run certain commands automatically before and after the
installation of the OS through script files called preinstall and postload that
you place alongside your install.cdf file.

Nice, easy and simple.

________________________
Jeff Thibault
Integraphic Inc.

