I'm not trying to increase the flames either, but I don't think that
it's correct at all to claim "AIX is also notorious for not being
compliant with UNIX standards".  

My understanding is that AIX meets all requirements to be branded UNIX
and that it tends to be among the first to certify with new SPEC
levels after they are ratified.  I recall several IBM press releases
stating that IBM was first to meet the blah-blah spec and such.  Is
AIX missing compliance with any major specifications?

I think the real issue is that AIX does things differently than other
UNIX variants that don't affect standards compliance.  Folks used to
editing system files in /etc don't take to using SMIT commands for
systems administration.  

 
