matsaki@statcan.ca wrote:
> 
> Hi!
> 
> I'm trying to figure out how to disable Port 1 (serial port on DEC Alpha---
> /dev/tty0 i believe)under  DU4.0D ... I'm not sure how I go about doing so..
> I'm trying to install Powerchute Plus (UPS monitoring software), and the
> manual says I have to disable the port...  The manual says to edit the
> inittab and make sure that the port i wish to use is set to OFF rather than
> RESPAWN... I have no entry for /dev/tty0 in my inittab...

Don't panic.

The manual is a bit unclear about that. So, you can have three things in inittab
for your COMx line.

1. A line with "respawn". It is usually an active login proces, which monitors
that line (getty or something like that). You should either remove it or put
"off" insted of "respawn" to shut it off. Don't forget "init q" to re-read
inittab. THIS IS NOT YOUR CASE.

2. A line with "off". It is a deactivated login process. No further actions
required. AGAIN, NOT YOUR CASE.

3. No line refering to "/dev/tty00" or "/dev/tty01". There's nothing monitoring
your serial line, no action required. THIS IS YOUR CASE.

In other words, just install it, it's OK.

Nix.




