Eric Werme - replace nospam with werme (nospam@zk3.dec.com) wrote:
: Mario Zimmermann <mzi2sn@sn0967.sn.bosch.de> writes:

: >we use nfs-file-locking.
: >Is there a way figure out, who has a lock on a file?
: >OS: Digital Unix 4.0d

: No.

Wrong. There are several ways of figuring out who has an NFS lock
on a file. You can either walk kernel lock tables, or you can use
the F_GETLK/F_RGETLK fcntl() interface. The latter case is trivial,
and Vic Abell's lslk will do the first one for you.

In either case, you'll get the PID of the process holding the lock,
and may get the IP number of the machine the said process is
running on. Given this, figuring out whatever else you may need
is trivial.

lslk is available at:

vic.cc.purdue.edu:pub/tools/unix/lslk

Cheers,

/Serge.P



