Hi,

a question re DUNIX 4.0d and LSM, running AdvFs (but not
advfs-utilities)
Can someone tell me if there is a correct way to do this:

Scenario: I have a filesystem which is an Advfs fileset, mirrored via
LSM.
It needs extending, and there is no more space available on this disk.

As we don't have advfs utilities I can use the growfs. My idea to do
this on the fly was this: Plug in two new disks and makedev to see them.
Works OK. Add them to LSM. Dissociate
one of the plexes from the original LSM volume. Make a new larger plex
from the new disk. Associate this plex to the old volume, when the
mirroring is done, then dissociate the other original plex, and mirror
again to the other new disk.

Problem is that even though the new plex is large enough, the volume is
still the original size.
What I finally did was to again dissociate the new larger plex from the
volume, unmount the filesystem, make a new larger volume using the new
plex. But now I couldn't use the volume until I had done a volume init
active. And when mounting it the data was gone. Of course I had tarred
it so no problem... But could I have done it without unmounting ? Or if
not could I have kept the data on the new plex, thus avoiding restore?

Rgds,
Hans Westerback
Ericsson Data

