Vinay Hegde wrote:
> 
> Sorry forgot to mention that these messages are not in the system log.
> 
> Vinay Hegde wrote:
> 
> > Hi,
> >         I have a DEC Alpha 4100 running DU4.0D. I would like to capture
> > error messages on the console  which scrolls pretty fast to read it.
> > Could somebody suggest me a  way to capture this and how?.

All messages, including those from boot screen are in one of these files:

/var/adm/messages			- boot messages, general complaints.
/var/adm/syslog.dated/<DATE>/mail.log	- E-Mail.
/var/adm/syslog.dated/<DATE>/kernel.log	- kernel complaints.
/var/adm/syslog.dated/<DATE>/daemon.log	- all system daemons.
/var/adm/syslog.dated/<DATE>/user.log	- other (like APC PowerChute)

Anyhow, you can see your configuration in /etc/syslog.conf

Nix.




