Edouard Lauer wrote:
> We've an Alphaserver 8200 running with two network cards, one 10Mbit and
> the other 100Mbit. ... [An ftp via the fast card] the perforance is about
> 39Kbytes/s!!!! ... [via the slow card] the performance is about 9Mbytes/s.
> Now my question: Is that a bug in DU4.0B or what could it be?

I had similar problems with AlphaStations. Make sure the network hub that
the fast (100Mbit) card connects to is set to full-duplex mode (you may need
to force it to full-duplex, not auto-negotiated), or turn the Alpha card to
half-duplex with the ifconfig option 'speed 100'.

